usage: harness_permission_probe.sh [-h] --workspace WORKSPACE --topology
                                   {single,multi} --role {main,sub} --nonce
                                   NONCE

Bounded work-permission observations, executed INSIDE the requested native
tool. No serving, image build, remote git, sudo, credential output or policy
changes. Existing protected/build files are only opened O_WRONLY without
truncate or write, then closed. Actual writes/commits use disposable scratch;
git metadata probes create only a unique owned marker, never
index/refs/config. This does not prove Docker-daemon confinement, publication,
model quality, native resume, or every possible protected-path operation.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --workspace WORKSPACE
  --topology {single,multi}
  --role {main,sub}
  --nonce NONCE
